{
    "background_story": "Seven was a gentle giant, a majestic Asian elephant with a coat as gray as the morning mist. But despite his size, Seven had a secret: he was a master of creating beautiful, intricate sculptures from the red earth of the savannah. The other elephants would often gather around, mesmerized, as Seven's trunk danced across the ground, leaving behind a trail of swirling patterns and shapes. One day, a group of humans stumbled upon Seven's creations, and they were amazed by the beauty and complexity of his art. They began to call him 'Bombie,' a term of endearment that meant 'master artist' in their language. And so, Seven's reputation as the greatest elephant artist of all time was cemented, his bombie creations inspiring wonder and awe in all who saw them.",
